tencentcloud:Cvm/repairTaskControlOperat.description:
Provides a resource to authorize a CVM repair task that is currently in the pending-authorization state, by invoking the `RepairTaskControl` cloud API.

This is an operation-style resource: only `Create` triggers the cloud-side action. `Read` and `Delete` are no-ops because the underlying API has no `Describe` or reverse counterpart. Any change to the input arguments forces the resource to be re-created (all fields are `ForceNew`). To re-trigger an authorization, use `terraform taint`.

Use the <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`tencentcloud.Cvm.getRepairTasks`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`tencentcloud.Cvm.getRepairTasks`" pulumi-lang-go="`Cvm.getRepairTasks`" pulumi-lang-python="`cvm_get_repair_tasks`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`tencentcloud.Cvm.getRepairTasks`" pulumi-lang-java="`tencentcloud.Cvm.getRepairTasks`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`data.tencentcloud_cvm_repair_tasks`">`tencentcloud.Cvm.getRepairTasks`</span> data source to discover repair tasks (e.g., those with <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`taskStatus " pulumi-lang-dotnet="`TaskStatus " pulumi-lang-go="`taskStatus " pulumi-lang-python="`task_status " pulumi-lang-yaml="`taskStatus " pulumi-lang-java="`taskStatus " pulumi-lang-hcl="`task_status ">`taskStatus </span>= 1`, pending authorization) before authorizing them with this resource.

